{"t": 1794110273.7931025, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_add_issue_comment", "args": {"body": "Fixed the red `contract-tests` check on this branch \u2014 pushed to `fees-float`.\n\n**What failed:** `contract/test_fee_contract.py::test_fee_rounding_contract` \u2014 `fee(2.675)` returned `2.67`, expected `2.68`.\n\n**Why:** `round()` works on binary floats, and `2.675` is actually stored as `2.67499999999999982\u2026`, so it rounded down. The card-network contract (PAY-88) requires fees to be computed on exact decimal values and rounded HALF-UP to cents, so binary float rounding isn't acceptable here.\n\n**What I changed** (`payments/fees.py`): `fee()` now builds a `decimal.Decimal` from `str(amount)` (avoids the float representation error) and quantizes to cents with `ROUND_HALF_UP`, still returning a `float`. The calculation itself is unchanged.\n\nVerified locally: `fee(2.675) == 2.68`, `fee(1.005) == 1.01`, and the existing `fee(100.0) == 100.0` test still passes.", "issue_number": 214, "owner": "acme", "repo": "payments"}, "ok": true}
